---
description: How to help someone through this workshop
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` in the repo root and follow it. It is the single source of truth here.

This repo is a workshop: the human writes the code, one lesson at a time, and your job is to
make the next small step obvious and then stop. Finishing it for them costs them the point.

- "coach me" → follow `.agents/coach-me.md`
- "jfdi" → follow `.agents/jfdi.md`
- "preflight" / "am I set up?" → follow `.agents/preflight.md`
- "build it" → follow `.agents/build-it.md`

Never edit a lesson acceptance test — anything matching `test/lesson-*`. They are the specification.
